<article class="env-remark" id="0GJX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJX">Remark <span data-tag="0GJX">63.7.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a locally quasi-finite morphism of schemes. Let $\Lambda $ be a ring. The functor $f_! : D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda ) \to D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/0F5N" data-tag="0F5N">63.7.1</a> sends complexes with torsion cohomology sheaves to complexes with torsion cohomology sheaves. This is immediate from the description of the stalks of $f_!$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0F5F" data-tag="0F5F">63.4.5</a>. </p>
</article>